<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="git-addon-configure">
  <title>Configure the Git Client</title>
  <shortdesc>Adjust how the Git Client behaves through its preferences pages, validation options, and
    editor variables.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>configuring</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <conbody>
    <p>The Git Client contributes several preferences pages to <ph keyref="product"/>, under
      <menucascade>
        <uicontrol conkeyref="pref-uicontrols/pref-options"/>
        <uicontrol conkeyref="pref-uicontrols/pref-preferences"/>
        <uicontrol conkeyref="pref-uicontrols/pref-plugins"/>
        <uicontrol conkeyref="pref-uicontrols/pref-git-client"/>
      </menucascade>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><xref href="git-addon-preferences.dita"/> - General behavior and validation.</li>
      <li><xref href="git-addon-ssh-preferences.dita"/> - SSH agent and passphrase.</li>
      <li><xref href="git-addon-ai-preferences.dita"/> - AI instructions and context limits.</li>
      <li><xref href="git-addon-credentials-preferences.dita"/> - Stored HTTP and token
        credentials.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can also <xref href="git-addon-validate-before-commit-push.dita">validate files before you
        commit or push</xref>, and use <xref href="git-addon-editor-variables.dita">Git editor
        variables</xref> in scenarios and templates.</p>
  </conbody>
</concept>
